[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m inside the [38;5;153m<main>[39m element:

  [90m<[34mlabel[90m>[39m
    [90m<[34minput[90m [36mtype[90m=[31m"checkbox"[90m [36mname[90m=[31m"done"[90m>[39m
    Done
  [90m</[34mlabel[90m>[39m

  It's a plain HTML checkbox, so the browser handles the on/off state and no JavaScript is needed. Because it's wrapped
  in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, clicking the word "Done" toggles it too.

  It doesn't save anything, so the state resets when the page reloads. I haven't opened it in a browser or committed it.
  If you want the done state to persist (for example with [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m) or want one checkbox per task, I can add that.

